            },
            "skip": {
                "php": "The reference gates the prompt path on PHP truthiness, so an empty prompt produces a request with NO user message — a behaviour the ports deliberately do not reproduce. Recorded rather than deleted, because the divergence is the finding: see docs/decisions/0002-idiom-vs-identity.md and finding F-2 in README.md. trq-0022 pins the same rule in a form every implementation agrees on."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "trq-0022",
            "title": "prompt that is exactly the string zero",
            "since": "0.1.0",
            "notes": "The string zero is falsy in PHP and in JavaScript but is ordinary model input. This row found a live defect in the reference on the corpus's first run: PendingRequest::toRequest() gates the prompt path on PHP truthiness, so a prompt of \"0\" produces a request with an EMPTY input array and the user's turn never reaches the model. The reference's own falsy-zero fix (commit 0f4e8ae) reached the provider message maps and missed the entry point. The golden here is the CORRECT behaviour, hand-authored, and the reference is skipped until it agrees — see finding F-2.",
            "builder": [
                {
                    "call": "using",
                    "args": [
                        "openai",
                        "gpt-4o"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "call": "withPrompt",
                    "args": [
                        "0"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "expect": {
                "body_json": "{\"model\":\"gpt-4o\",\"input\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"0\"}]}],\"max_output_tokens\":null}"
            },
            "skip": {
                "php": "Known reference defect, not a language divergence: Text\\PendingRequest::toRequest() appends the prompt behind `if ($this->prompt)`, so a prompt that is exactly \"0\" is dropped and the request carries no user message at all. The golden records what the reference SHOULD produce; the port contract is the golden, not the defect. Remove this skip when the reference is fixed."
            }
